WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:05.140
Remoras, nature’s underwater hitchhikers, hold on tight

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:08.600
to jumping dolphins, boat hulls, even divers.

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:11.040
Also called suckerfish, their amazing grip

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:13.680
comes from an adhesive disk made from a modified

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.720
dorsal fin on the fish’s head.

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:17.840
So obviously, the question is--

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:20.560
could a robot be designed hold on this tight,

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:23.440
underwater, to different surfaces?

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:25.520
Making something that works like a remora’s disk

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:27.880
will help us better understand how they work

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:31.120
and could one day lead to useful underwater
devices

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:33.840
based on the same principles.

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:36.040
Researchers took up the challenge and designed

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:38.680
a “biomimetic remora disk”

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:40.680
Like the fish’s specialized sucker,

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:43.680
it can make a seal and has rows of flaps,

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:45.520
dotted with tiny spikes,

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:49.060
that allow it to raise and lower the area under the seal.

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:50.680
To test out how well this sucker worked,

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:52.140
researchers attached it to

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:53.800
a remote controlled controlled submarine,

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:56.040
and tested out its capabilities.

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:57.820
On average, the sucker grabbed onto

00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:00.860
plexiglass and sharkskin in less than four seconds,

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:02.720
and held on tight.

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:06.280
Once stuck, It took 45 kilograms of force to remove it.

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:08.540
That’s about 340 times the weight

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:10.600
of the prototype sucker.

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:14.100
It also stayed sticky outside of the water as well

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:16.300
In the future, researchers hope to see

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:18.280
similar suction systems used anywhere

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:19.980
strong adhesion is needed

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:22.000
and at some point used to extend

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:23.760
the range of robotic submarines.

